227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 103 0 R
/T (Yet again, a separate mixed-methods study among internally displaced women in Central Ethiopia found that nearly one-third of women had experienced GBV, with almost 80 percent of incidents occurring within IDP camps themselves rather than during flight \(Mitiku et al., 2025\). All these findings bear direct relevance to this brief's recommendation that displacement responses must treat camp and settlement environments as protection priorities, not just transit risks.)
/E (Yet again, a separate mixed-methods study among internally displaced women in Central Ethiopia found that nearly one-third of women had experienced GBV, with almost 80 percent of incidents occurring within IDP camps themselves rather than during flight \(Mitiku et al., 2025\). All these findings bear direct relevance to this brief's recommendation that displacement responses must treat camp and settlement environments as protection priorities, not just transit risks.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 103 0 R
/T (The compounding effect of disability alongside gender and climate vulnerability, identified throughout this study, is corroborated by recent academic work specifically focused on Eastern Africa. A study of women with disabilities across the region found significant barriers to evacuation, access to early-warning systems, inclusive infrastructure and policy participation, while also documenting resilience through community support networks and adaptive household practices. The same study notes that national climate policies, including Nationally Determined Contributions \(NDCs\) and National Adaptation Plans \(NAPs\) rarely address the specific needs of women with disabilities at all. )
/E (The compounding effect of disability alongside gender and climate vulnerability, identified throughout this study, is corroborated by recent academic work specifically focused on Eastern Africa. A study of women with disabilities across the region found significant barriers to evacuation, access to early-warning systems, inclusive infrastructure and policy participation, while also documenting resilience through community support networks and adaptive household practices. The same study notes that national climate policies, including Nationally Determined Contributions \(NDCs\) and National Adaptation Plans \(NAPs\) rarely address the specific needs of women with disabilities at all. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 103 0 R
/T (This gap between documented need and policy attention is precisely the pattern this brief's intersectionality findings describe. Taken together, this literature confirms that our findings reflect well-established regional patterns: pastoral mobility is genuinely diversifying into distinct forms with different risk profiles; displaced women face substantial, quantifiable GBV risk that often peaks after arrival rather than only during flight; and disability-inclusive analysis remains largely absent from the climate and mobility policy frameworks that are supposed to protect the most vulnerable.)
/E (This gap between documented need and policy attention is precisely the pattern this brief's intersectionality findings describe. Taken together, this literature confirms that our findings reflect well-established regional patterns: pastoral mobility is genuinely diversifying into distinct forms with different risk profiles; displaced women face substantial, quantifiable GBV risk that often peaks after arrival rather than only during flight; and disability-inclusive analysis remains largely absent from the climate and mobility policy frameworks that are supposed to protect the most vulnerable.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
