/T (Respondents described a shift from planned seasonal mobility toward longer migration routes, rural-to-urban migration, movement into IDP settlements, and cross-border mobility. In Somalia, displacement and settlement in IDP sites were especially prominent; in Kenya and Tanzania, disruption of traditional grazing routes and longer-distance movement were more frequently emphasized. This diversification of mobility forms was reported by key informants across all four study countries, though the dominant form varies by national context.)
/E (Respondents described a shift from planned seasonal mobility toward longer migration routes, rural-to-urban migration, movement into IDP settlements, and cross-border mobility. In Somalia, displacement and settlement in IDP sites were especially prominent; in Kenya and Tanzania, disruption of traditional grazing routes and longer-distance movement were more frequently emphasized. This diversification of mobility forms was reported by key informants across all four study countries, though the dominant form varies by national context.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
