/P 105 0 R
/E (Displaced women frequently lose access to the customary resource rights and informal social-protection systems that would otherwise support them during crisis i.e. rights and systems that are, in many pastoral contexts, tied closely to physical presence within a specific community or territory. This loss compounds the material hardship of displacement itself. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (The Research and Evidence Facility's regional analysis notes that policy responses to climate-linked mobility in the Horn of Africa have often prioritized sedentarization and alternative livelihoods over protecting the mobility - dependent rights and systems that pastoral communities, including women specifically, have historically relied on \(Research and Evidence Facility, 2022\). We find that this policy orientation deepens rather than reduces the vulnerability of displaced women.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
