264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 106 0 R
/E (While protection concerns during migration itself i.e. unsafe travel, exploitation en route / in transit is well recognized, the evidence base indicates that risk does not end on arrival. For instance, a mixed-methods study of internally displaced women in Central Ethiopia found that nearly 80 percent of GBV incidents occurred within IDP camps themselves, primarily perpetrated by intimate partners and family members, rather than during flight \(\(Mitiku et al, 2025\). )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 106 0 R
/E (Elsewhere, a separate cross-sectional study in Northwest Ethiopia found a one-year GBV prevalence of 37.9 percent among internally displaced women, with young women and those lacking social protection at significantly elevated risk Workie et al, 2023\). )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 106 0 R
/E (These findings have direct implications for how displacement responses are designed, specifically that camp and settlement environments require sustained, structural protection programming, not only transit-phase interventions focused on the journey itself.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
