/E (The recommendations below are derived directly from the key informant interview findings presented in this brief and are further supported by the regional and global literature reviewed above. They translate this brief's core argument, that mobility, displacement and staying-behind require distinct protection responses, not a single generic mobility policy into specific institutional actions, naming the mechanism, the responsible actors, and existing standards to adopt.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 108 0 R
/T (1. Disaggregated Mobility Policy)
/E (1. Disaggregated Mobility Policy)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 618 0 R
/E (Disaggregate mobility policy by movement type - design distinct protection and support responses for planned pastoral mobility, forced displacement, sedentarization and labour or educational migration, rather than a single generic mobility policy, following the analytical distinctions established in the regional academic literature \(Etzold, 2023\).)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 619 0 R
/E (Support women who stay behind, not only those who move - recognize and resource the household and community burden absorbed by women who remain in place as mobile household members migrate, including support for social networks that disperse during displacement.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 108 0 R
/T (2. Protection Programming Beyond Transit)
/E (2. Protection Programming Beyond Transit)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 620 0 R
/E (Resource GBV prevention specifically for camp and settlement environments - ensure GBV prevention and response services are funded and staffed for post-arrival settings specifically, given documented evidence that a substantial share of GBV incidents against displaced women occur after arrival rather than during flight.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 621 0 R
/E (Apply established GBV coordination standards from the point of settlement - implement the Inter-Agency Standing Committee \(IASC\) Minimum Standards for GBV prevention and response from the earliest stage of camp or settlement establishment, rather than treating GBV programming as a later addition to shelter and food response.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 108 0 R
/T (3. Preserving Rights Through Displacement)
/E (3. Preserving Rights Through Displacement)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 622 0 R
/E (Protect customary resource rights through displacement - develop mechanisms that preserve or restore displaced women's access to customary resource rights and social-protection systems, rather than treating these as automatically forfeited upon displacement.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 108 0 R
/T (POLICY RECOMMENDATIONS)
/E (POLICY RECOMMENDATIONS)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
