/T (4. Disability-Disaggregated Data and Inclusion)
/E (4. Disability-Disaggregated Data and Inclusion)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 626 0 R
/E (Adopt the Washington Group Short Set as the standard disaggregation tool - require humanitarian and displacement data systems operating in pastoral areas to use the Washington Group Short Set on Functioning i.e. the tool already standardized by WFP and endorsed jointly by UNICEF, WHO and UNDP for disability data disaggregation to close the current data gap that prevents accurate identification of compounded vulnerability.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 627 0 R
/E (Integrate disability inclusion into climate and mobility policy directly - ensure National Adaptation Plans, Nationally Determined Contributions and displacement-response frameworks explicitly address the needs of women with disabilities, closing a gap the literature identifies. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 109 0 R
/T (5. Intersectional Protection Design)
/E (5. Intersectional Protection Design)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 628 0 R
/E (Build intersectional protection protocols - design protection services that explicitly account for intersecting / compounding vulnerabilities e.g. widowhood, disability, age, minority-clan status, rather than using single-axis gender programming alone.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
