/P 110 0 R
/T (This brief is the fourth in a five-part CGIAR- OPPD -SAWONET policy brief series drawing on key informant interviews with pastoralist women-led, humanitarian, climate-resilience and peacebuilding organizations across Kenya, Somalia, Tanzania and South Africa. It builds on the flagship brief's overarching findings \(Brief 1\), the adaptation-leadership evidence in Brief 2, and the rangeland governance and peacebuilding findings in Brief 3 and precedes the companion brief on aligning education systems with pastoral mobility.)
/E (This brief is the fourth in a five-part CGIAR- OPPD -SAWONET policy brief series drawing on key informant interviews with pastoralist women-led, humanitarian, climate-resilience and peacebuilding organizations across Kenya, Somalia, Tanzania and South Africa. It builds on the flagship brief's overarching findings \(Brief 1\), the adaptation-leadership evidence in Brief 2, and the rangeland governance and peacebuilding findings in Brief 3 and precedes the companion brief on aligning education systems with pastoral mobility.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
