1288 0 obj
<<
/Title (Yet again, a separate mixed-methods study among internally displaced women in Central Ethiopia found that nearly one-third of women had experienced GBV, with almost 80 percent of incidents occurring within IDP camps themselves rather than during flight \(Mitiku et al., 2025\). All these findings bear direct relevance to this brief's recommendation that displacement responses must treat camp and settlement environments as protection priorities, not just transit risks.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1283 0 R
/Next 1289 0 R
>>
endobj
1289 0 obj
<<
/Title (The compounding effect of disability alongside gender and climate vulnerability, identified throughout this study, is corroborated by recent academic work specifically focused on Eastern Africa. A study of women with disabilities across the region found significant barriers to evacuation, access to early-warning systems, inclusive infrastructure and policy participation, while also documenting resilience through community support networks and adaptive household practices. The same study notes that national climate policies, including Nationally Determined Contributions \(NDCs\) and National Adaptation Plans \(NAPs\) rarely address the specific needs of women with disabilities at all.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1288 0 R
/Next 1284 0 R
>>
endobj
1290 0 obj
<<
/Title (Respondents described a shift from planned seasonal mobility toward longer migration routes, rural-to-urban migration, movement into IDP settlements, and cross-border mobility. In Somalia, displacement and settlement in IDP sites were especially prominent; in Kenya and Tanzania, disruption of traditional grazing routes and longer-distance movement were more frequently emphasized. This diversification of mobility forms was reported by key informants across all four study countries, though the dominant form varies by national context.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1285 0 R
/Next 1291 0 R
>>
endobj
1291 0 obj
<<
/Title (This distinction is precisely what Etzold's \(2023\) intersecting \(im\)mobilities framework captures i.e. pastoral mobility, sedentarization, forced displacement and labour or educational migration are occurring simultaneously across Horn of Africa communities, each shaped differently by drought and conflict, rather than pastoral movement simply being replaced wholesale by displacement.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1285 0 R
/Prev 1290 0 R
>>
endobj
